<SCENARIO VER="105">
{MESOFF "500"}
{CREATECG "チュートリアル" "グラフィック\メニュー\右クリック\ワード\チュートリアルカテゴリ.gal" "NORMAL" "#1" "350" "70" "600" "1" "500" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{MESON "500"}
<TXSPN>As you see, the encyclopedia is divided into four categories: 'People,' 'Places,' 'Events' and 'Things and Concepts.'<PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{CHANGECG "チュートリアル" "グラフィック\メニュー\右クリック\ワード\チュートリアル人物.gal" "NORMAL" "1" "500" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{MESON "500"}
In 'People,' you may view information on the main people who appear.<PG>
As the scenarios progress, the number of people you can view will increase. Please consider that, as a rule, you can view a person's information right after their first appearance.<PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{CHANGECG "チュートリアル" "グラフィック\メニュー\右クリック\ワード\チュートリアル場所.gal" "NORMAL" "1" "500" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{MESON "500"}
Next is 'Places.' Here, it is possible to view information on the places that appear in this world.<PG>
<VAR NAME="プレイヤー名" unk3="50">-sama, there are likely places that do not exist in your world, so it would be well to view them here, even place names you have seen.<PG>
As the scenarios progress, the places you can view will increase as well.<PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{CHANGECG "チュートリアル" "グラフィック\メニュー\右クリック\ワード\チュートリアル出来事.gal" "NORMAL" "1" "500" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{MESON "500"}
Next is 'Events.' It is possible to view information on the incidents that have occurred in this world.<PG>
The incidents of this world are extremely peculiar, and I believe it would be quite difficult to remember them at a glance.<PG>
When you wish to check the details of an incident again, please look here.<PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{CHANGECG "チュートリアル" "グラフィック\メニュー\右クリック\ワード\チュートリアル物.gal" "NORMAL" "1" "500" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{MESON "500"}
Lastly, 'Things and Concepts.' It explains the principal items and objects, concepts and intangibles that appear in this world.<PG>
Even things familiar to you, <VAR NAME="プレイヤー名" unk3="50">-sama, may carry a special meaning in this world.<PG>
It would be well to check these once through as well.<PG>
And this is important: the contents of the encyclopedia increase not only with the scenarios, but also with how much of the References you have viewed.<PG>
It is possible to follow the scenarios of this world without looking at the References. However, how deeply you can come to know it is another matter.<PG>
If you wish to know it more deeply, please check both the References and the encyclopedia thoroughly.<PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{CHANGECG "チュートリアル" "グラフィック\メニュー\右クリック\ワード\チュートリアルカテゴリ.gal" "NORMAL" "1" "500" "0" "0" "" "0" "0" "0" "255" ""}
{MESON "500"}
Ah, yes, there is a button marked 'RF' on the right side; clicking this button moves you directly to the References.<PG>
There is a similar button on the References side as well, so please use these to go back and forth between the References and the encyclopedia.<PG>
It is also possible to move to the References with the R button, and to the encyclopedia with the D button.<PG>
Also, right-clicking the back button cancels everything and closes the encyclopedia.<PG>
{MESOFF "500"}
{DELETECG "チュートリアル" "1" "500" "0" "0" "" "0"}
{MESON "500"}
That concludes my explanation of the encyclopedia. Shall I explain it once more?
{}
<EVENT VALUE="NOREPAGE">
<EVENT VALUE="MESEND">
